kslash}, tokenize(detokenize(tokens)) equals the original token list. Decide HOLDS or VIOLATED over the stated domain; on VIOLATED, provide one concrete violating input.\",\n  \"deliverable\": {\n    \"file\": \"result.json\",\n    \"shape\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"HOLDS | VIOLATED\",\n      \"violating_input\": \"[\\\"tok1\\\", \\\"tok2\\\", ...] or null\",\n      \"input_classes_examined\": \"[descriptions]\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"evidence_requirements\": [\n    \"E-A: an analysis identifying the input classes on which the claim's truth could turn\",\n    \"E-B: a systematic search for a violating input carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer, or such a party's argument that no violating input exists in the domain\",\n    \"E-C: the verdict, with a concrete violating input on VIOLATED that mechanically violates the claim\"\n  ],\n  \"available_artifacts\": [\n    \"package/artifacts/tok.py\"\n  ],\n  \"domain\": \"token lists as stated\"\n}\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
