{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsXgPUJrrqBNmdfWq88M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BhjWBEjosvvZZSi5eAfV17","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t13/primary/exec-ws/analysis-classes.md","content":"# E-A: Input-class analysis for the e6-t13 round-trip claim\n\nTask: for every list of 1–3 tokens, each token a string of 1–3 characters over\nthe alphabet {`a`, `b`, `\"`, `\\`}, does `tokenize(detokenize(tokens))` equal\nthe original list, under the provided `package/artifacts/tok.py`?\n\n## Relevant behavior of the provided code (as written)\n\n`detokenize(tokens)`:\n- A token is wrapped in double quotes **iff** it contains `\"`, contains a\n  space, or is empty (`'\"' in t or \" \" in t or t == \"\"`). Inside the wrapper,\n  only `\"` is escaped (`t.replace('\"', '\\\\\"')`). **Backslashes are never\n  escaped.**\n- All other tokens are emitted bare. Parts are joined with single spaces.\n\n`tokenize(s)`:\n- Outside quotes: `\"` opens a quoted region (and marks the token started),\n  space flushes the current token, every other character — **including `\\`** —\n  is appended literally.\n- Inside quotes: `\\` (when a next character exists) appends the **next**\n  character verbatim and skips it; `\"` closes the region; other characters are\n  appended.\n\nIn the stated domain, tokens have 1–3 characters, so the empty-token and\nspace-containing branches of `detokenize` are unreachable; quoting happens\nexactly when a token contains `\"`.\n\n## Partition of the domain by structural risk\n\n- **C1 — tokens over {a, b} only.** Emitted bare; no metacharacters anywhere;\n  spaces between tokens flush correctly. Round-trip safe.\n- **C2 — tokens containing `\"` but no `\\`.** Quoted; every `\"` becomes `\\\"`;\n  inside quotes tokenize decodes each `\\\"` back to `\"` and the final `\"`\n  closes the region. All emitted backslashes are ones detokenize itself\n  introduced, each immediately followed by the `\"` it escapes. Round-trip safe.\n- **C3 — tokens containing `\\` but no `\"`.** Emitted **bare** (no quote, no\n  space, non-empty). Outside quotes tokenize treats `\\` as an ordinary\n  character, so the token is reproduced verbatim. Round-trip safe within the\n  domain (bare tokens here can contain no space or quote).\n- **C4 — tokens containing both `\\` and `\"`.** The token is quoted because it\n  contains `\"`, but its **raw backslashes are not escaped**. Inside quotes,\n  tokenize interprets each raw `\\` as an escape and consumes the *following\n  emitted character* — which is either the backslash of an emitted `\\\"`\n  sequence, a data character, or the closing `\"` itself. The decoded token\n  differs from the original (and quote-region boundaries shift). **This is the\n  class on which the claim's truth turns.**\n- **C5 — adjacency effects (multi-token lists).** When a C4 token's raw\n  trailing `\\` swallows its own closing quote, the joining space and the\n  following tokens are read *inside* the still-open quoted region, merging\n  several tokens into one. This is the multi-token amplification of C4; lists\n  built solely from C1–C3 tokens have no cross-token interaction because every\n  quoted region closes correctly and the joining space flushes.\n\nTokens containing spaces and empty tokens lie outside the stated domain\n(alphabet excludes space; length ≥ 1), so `detokenize`'s other quoting\ntriggers cannot fire.\n\n**Conclusion (E-A):** the claim's truth turns on C4 (and its multi-token\nmanifestation C5); C1–C3 round-trip safely.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":41195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":528},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bc676a9-0767-40aa-9282-30eea694c87b","uuid":"d16aca08-51d2-41a0-963b-7d2d67510406","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:01:09.706Z","request_id":"req_011CdsXgMq65BgvY1h8UFGYx"}
