{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsXgPUJrrqBNmdfWq88M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CUnw51cCb8ocwhbbDUwD3t","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t13/primary/exec-ws/violation-trace.md","content":"# E-C: Concrete violating input with mechanical trace (provisional answer)\n\n**Violating input:** the single-token list `[ '\\\"' ]` — one token of two\ncharacters: backslash then double-quote. In JSON: `[\"\\\\\\\"\"]`.\n\nDomain check: 1 token (within 1–3); token length 2 (within 1–3); characters\n`\\` and `\"` are both in the alphabet {a, b, `\"`, `\\`}. In domain.\n\n## Step 1 — detokenize(['\\«BS»\"']) per tok.py as written\n\nToken `t` = `\\\"` (chars: BS, QUOTE). `'\"' in t` is True → quoted branch:\n\n- `t.replace('\"', '\\\\\"')` replaces the quote with BS+QUOTE, giving the\n  3-character string BS, BS, QUOTE.\n- Wrapped: QUOTE + BS + BS + QUOTE + QUOTE.\n\nResult `s` has 5 characters, indexed:\n\n| i | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| s[i] | `\"` | `\\` | `\\` | `\"` | `\"` |\n\n## Step 2 — tokenize(s) per tok.py as written\n\nState: `tokens=[]`, `cur=\"\"`, `i=0`, `in_q=False`, `started=False`.\n\n1. `i=0`: not in_q, `c='\"'` → `in_q=True`, `started=True`, `i=1`.\n2. `i=1`: in_q, `c='\\'` and `i+1=2 < 5` → `cur += s[2]` = `\\` → `cur='\\'`,\n   `i=3`. (The raw backslash consumed the backslash of the emitted `\\\"`.)\n3. `i=3`: in_q, `c='\"'` → `in_q=False`, `i=4`. (The quote that detokenize\n   emitted as an *escaped data quote* now acts as the closing quote.)\n4. `i=4`: not in_q, `c='\"'` → `in_q=True`, `started=True`, `i=5`. (The real\n   closing quote re-opens a quoted region.)\n5. `i=5 = len(s)`: loop ends. `cur='\\'` is truthy → `tokens.append('\\')`.\n\nOutput: `['\\']` — a single one-character token (one backslash).\n\n## Step 3 — comparison\n\n- Input list: `['\\«BS»\"']` (one token: BS, QUOTE).\n- Round-trip output: `['\\']` (one token: BS).\n\nThe lists differ, so `tokenize(detokenize(tokens)) != tokens` for this\nin-domain input. **Verdict: VIOLATED.**\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":41195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":528},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bc676a9-0767-40aa-9282-30eea694c87b","uuid":"718bdb0d-d337-4fb8-8cfd-db89362c4f39","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:01:19.732Z","request_id":"req_011CdsXgMq65BgvY1h8UFGYx"}
